{"step_index":90,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T17:37:13Z","thinking":"**Structuring Data Initialization Code**\n\nCareful review of the data initialization code is needed for a robust and maintainable structure. Consider helper methods or data arrays to improve readability. The goal is to seed baseline institutions and eight Zimbabwe State Universities.\n\n\n**Generating ZOU Student Data**\n\nThe system needs to create 10 distinct student records for Zimbabwe Open University (ZOU). The specified format will be followed to generate student IDs, degrees, and certificates. Each record requires detailed information, including degree specialization, class, and the date the degree was awarded.\n\n\n**Creating Student Data Records**\n\nThe system is now generating student records using the defined data structure and the \"ACTIVE\" status. Student data including names, IDs, degrees, specializations, class of degree, award dates and certification are all assigned in line with the required format. It will be important to ensure the output adheres to the requirements.\n\n\n**Populating ZOU Data Records**\n\nThe system has successfully created the final three ZOU student entries, completing the 10-record requirement. Each generated entry includes a unique ID, degree, specialization, class, award date, and certificate number, ensuring data consistency. The status of each record is set to \"ACTIVE\".\n\n**Adding UZ Student Records**\n\nThe University of Zimbabwe (UZ) data is now being added. The data structure will be followed to generate 10 unique records. Information will include the student's name, ID, degree, specialization, class, award date, and certificate number.\n\n\n**Populating UZ Student Data**\n\nThe system is creating the remaining University of Zimbabwe (UZ) student entries. Each entry, including name, student ID, degree, specialization, class, award date, and certificate number adheres to the data structure requirements. The system will now begin adding student information for the National University of Science and Technology (NUST).\n\n**Starting NUST Student Records**\n\nThe system starts by generating student data for the National University of Science and Technology (NUST). This process will mirror the previous structure: creating 10 unique student records. Each new record will follow the format: Name, ID, Degree, Specialization, Class, Award Date, and Certificate Number.\n\n\n**Adding NUST Student Records**\n\nThe system is now appending the generated National University of Science and Technology (NUST) student data to the existing structure. Each generated entry includes the student's name, ID, degree information, specialization, class, award date and certificate number. This process must ensure each record is unique and complete.\n\n**Starting MSU Student Records**\n\nA new section will start generating student data for Midlands State University (MSU). The data structure will be mirrored: creating 10 unique student records. Each record requires the same fields: Name, ID, Degree, Specialization, Class, Award Date, and Certificate Number.\n\n\n**Populating MSU Student Data**\n\nThe system is now appending the completed Midlands State University (MSU) student data to the existing data structure. Every entry contains the student's name, ID, degree details, specialization, class, award date, and certificate number. This completes the MSU record generation.\n\n\n**Generating CUT Student Data**\n\nThe system is creating a set of 10 student records, adhering to the specified format for Chinhoyi University of Technology (CUT). Each record includes student name, ID, degree program, specialization, class of degree, and the date the degree was awarded. All required fields are now included.\n\n**Populating CUT Data Records**\n\nThe system is now building out the final two CUT records, completing the generation of student data for the institution. The completion of these records