{"step_index":94,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T17:39:44Z","thinking":"**Structuring Data Initialization**\n\nConsidering updating the data initializer to populate the Zimbabwe State Universities and student data. A well-organized structure is crucial for managing the records. Define helper arrays or records to handle the data.\n\n\n**Confirming Java Version and Method Design**\n\nVerified Java 17 compatibility. Designing helper methods for seeding institutions, qualifications, and user accounts. The suggested method structure for seeding an institution appears clean, robust, and effective for data population.\n\n**Listing Institution Data**\n\nListing out institution details including Zimbabwe Open University (ZOU) with its information. Preparing to map each institution and associated qualifications.\n\n\n**Mapping Student Data to Qualification**\n\nAnalyzing the student data and matching it with corresponding qualifications. Constructed a data structure that mirrors the given student records, and created an approach to associate each entry with a university and degree details. This should provide a clean way to integrate this data.\n\n\n**Populating Institution Data Structures**\n\nNow populating the data structures with both Zimbabwe Open University (ZOU) and the University of Zimbabwe (UZ) details, ensuring qualifications and corresponding student records are correctly associated. The goal is to accurately represent the hierarchical relationships between institutions, qualifications and students.\n\nEvaluating how to accurately insert student records to qualifications, carefully mapping each data point. This could be where the approach might need to be adjusted if the data structures can't be adapted.\n\n\n**Adding Student and University Data**\n\nNow processing the provided student data, specifically focusing on the University of Zimbabwe (UZ) entries. The goal is to accurately map students to their respective qualifications and institutions. Initial suspicion is that degree program and specialization data will require additional preprocessing, or mapping steps.\n\n\n**Analyzing NUST Data Structure**\n\nNow, integrating the National University of Science and Technology (NUST) data. Examining the structure of the provided data for degrees to map and match data points to existing structures. The initial focus is on the degree records, which seem to include unique identifiers, student names, and qualification details.\n\n**Mapping NUST Degrees to Data Model**\n\nSuccessfully mapping NUST degree records to the data structure. Considering potential data type inconsistencies for dates and grades and checking the need for pre-processing steps. The mapping confirms the correct association with institution and degree information.\n\n\n**Integrating MSU Data Structures**\n\nIntegrating the Midlands State University (MSU) data, adding its details into the system. Mapping the degree records, student names, qualification, and relevant attributes to the previously defined structures. Now the mapping is focused on ensuring the integrity of the data.\n\n**Identifying Data Structure Mismatches**\n\nThe date format requires adjustment to avoid data type mismatches, focusing on the processing of dates. The format from the provided data needs to be verified and standardized. Further data type checks are crucial for the degree classification to ensure correct data insertion.\n\n\n**Matching MSU data with Data Model**\n\nNow matching the Midlands State University (MSU) student data to the degree records. Identifying and mapping individual student entries to their respective degrees, ensuring data consistency across fields. The focus is to integrate the student details including qualification and registration information.\n\n\n**Integrating CUT Data Structures**\n\nNow incorporating the Chinhoyi University of Technology (CUT) data. Carefully reviewing the degree records to accurately map each student's information to existing data structures. The current focus is on correctly parsing the provided data and fitting it to the existing degree details.\n\n**Matching CUT Data Points**\n\nIdentifying and mapping the relevant data points from CUT's data to the system. Analyzing degree titles, student names, and qualification details. Need to ensure data integrity during the population of records, especially checking the date fields for compatibility.\n\n\n**Adding BUSE Data to the Model**\n\nNow incorporating Bindura University of Science Education (BUSE) data into the system, focusing on its degrees and student details. Parsing student degree data and validating date formats for consistency within the existing records. Ensuring the data integrates accurately with current models.\n\n**Refining Date Parsing and Formatting**\n\nFurther refining the date parsing logic to ensure compatibility across all institution data, handling inconsistencies. The goal is to provide a consistent date format for all student records. Need to evaluate the correct data types to prevent errors during data entry.\n\n\n**Finalizing BUSE Student Data Integration**\n\nNow integrating the remaining BUSE student records into existing data structures. Confirming all data fields are mapped correctly including degree classifications. Performing a final validation on the data to ensure data integrity.\n\n**Verifying Data Integrity Across Data Sets**\n\nDouble-checking the BUSE entries against previous university data, specifically date formats. Confirming that all data adheres to the new, consistent date format. This will ensure consistency and prevent errors during subsequent operations.\n\n\n**Integrating GZU Data**\n\nNow incorporating Great Zimbabwe University (GZU) data into the model, mapping its data to existing structures. Processing GZU's degrees by associating the given fields with the appropriate data model attributes, paying attention to registration details.\n\n**Matching GZU Data Fields**\n\nMatching the GZU student data to the degree records. Confirming date and grade consistency across the various fields. Verifying that the qualification data correctly matches the student's records.\n\n\n**Integrating HIT Data into Model**\n\nNow integrating the Harare Institute of Technology (HIT) data, mapping records to data structures. Focusing on parsing student data including degree and enrollment information. Verifying that the data is integrated appropriately into the model structure.\n\n**Mapping HIT Degree Records**\n\nMapping HIT's degree records to the previously established data structure, focusing on matching attributes correctly. Parsing and integrating the student information, including program details and other attributes. Need to ensure data integrity during population.\n\n\n**Validating HIT Data Structures**\n\nAnalyzing the HIT student data to ensure proper integration with the existing data model, focusing on validation. Confirming data integrity by cross-referencing degree classifications and registration data. The initial mapping looks consistent, but further checks are needed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Updates DataInitializer.java to seed 8 Zimbabwe State Universities and 80+ authentic qualifications across UZ, NUST, MSU, ZOU, CUT, BUSE, GZU, and HIT. Implements specific student ID formats for ZOU IT (ITM 190020) and ZOU PGDE (EH250001, where first two digits are the year). Cryptographically notarizes all records onto the blockchain ledger.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"package com.devops.qvs.config;\n\nimport com.devops.qvs.model.Institution;\nimport com.devops.qvs.model.Qualification;\nimport com.devops.qvs.model.QualificationStatus;\nimport com.devops.qvs.model.Role;\nimport com.devops.qvs.model.User;\nimport com.devops.qvs.repository.InstitutionRepository;\nimport com.devops.qvs.repository.QualificationRepository;\nimport com.devops.qvs.repository.UserRepository;\nimport com.devops.qvs.service.BlockchainLedgerService;\nimport com.devops.qvs.service.CryptoHashService;\nimport org.slf4j.Logger;\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\nimport org.springframework.boot.CommandLineRunner;\nimport org.springframework.security.crypto.password.PasswordEncoder;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n@Component\npublic class DataInitializer implements CommandLineRunner {\n\n    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(DataInitializer.class);\n\n    private final UserRepository userRepository;\n    private final InstitutionRepository institutionRepository;\n    private final QualificationRepository qualificationRepository;\n    private final PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder;\n    private final CryptoHashService cryptoHashService;\n    private final BlockchainLedgerService blockchainLedgerService;\n\n    public DataInitializer(UserRepository userRepository,\n                           InstitutionRepository institutionRepository,\n                           QualificationRepository qualificationRepository,\n                           PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder,\n                           CryptoHashService cryptoHashService,\n                           BlockchainLedgerService blockchainLedgerService) {\n        this.userRepository = userRepository;\n        this.institutionRepository = institutionRepository;\n        this.qualificationRepository = qualificationRepository;\n        this.passwordEncoder = passwordEncoder;\n        this.cryptoHashService = cryptoHashService;\n        this.blockchainLedgerService = blockchainLedgerService;\n    }\n\n    private record SeedRecord(\n            String certNum,\n            String studentName,\n            String studentId,\n            String awardTitle,\n            String specialization,\n            String classification,\n            LocalDate awardDate,\n            QualificationStatus status,\n            String revocationReason\n    ) {}\n\n    @Override\n    public void run(String... args) {\n        if (institutionRepository.count() == 0) {\n            logger.info(\"Initializing Comprehensive DevOps Qualification Data & Zimbabwe State Universities Ledger...\");\n\n            // 1. Core Users (Admin & Verifier)\n            userRepository.save(User.builder()\n                    .username(\"admin\")\n                    .email(\"admin@qvs.internal\")\n                    .password(passwordEncoder.encode(\"Admin@12345\"))\n                    .fullName(\"DevOps System Administrator\")\n                    .role(Role.ROLE_ADMIN)\n                    .enabled(true)\n                    .build());\n\n            userRepository.save(User.builder()\n                    .username(\"verifier\")\n                    .email(\"verifier@trusted-partner.org\")\n                    .password(passwordEncoder.encode(\"Verifier@12345\"))\n                    .fullName(\"Accredited Verification Agent\")\n                    .role(Role.ROLE_VERIFIER)\n                    .enabled(true)\n                    .build());\n\n            // 2. Baseline Demo Institutions & Qualifications (preserves test suite stability)\n            seedBaselineDemoInstitutions();\n\n            // 3. Zimbabwe State Universities & Qualifications (10 students each with distinct degrees)\n            seedZimbabweStateUniversities();\n\n            logger.info(\"Qualification Verification System successfully seeded with {} institutions and {} qualifications on blockchain ledger.\",\n                    institutionRepository.count(), qualificationRepository.count());\n        }\n    }\n\n    private void seedBaselineDemoInstitutions() {\n        Institution inst1 = institutionRepository.save(Institution.builder()\n                .name(\"National Institute of Technology\")\n                .institutionCode(\"NIT-001\")\n                .contactEmail(\"verify@nit.edu\")\n                .country(\"United Kingdom\")\n                .website(\"https://nit.edu\")\n                .build());\n\n        Institution inst2 = institutionRepository.save(Institution.builder()\n                .name(\"Metropolitan University\")\n                .institutionCode(\"METRO-002\")\n                .contactEmail(\"registry@metro.ac.uk\")\n                .country(\"United Kingdom\")\n                .website(\"https://metro.ac.uk\")\n                .build());\n\n        userRepository.save(User.builder()\n                .username(\"officer\")\n                .email(\"officer@nit.edu\")\n                .password(passwordEncoder.encode(\"Officer@12345\"))\n                .fullName(\"Academic Registrar Officer\")\n                .role(Role.ROLE_INSTITUTION)\n                .institution(inst1)\n                .enabled(true)\n                .build());\n\n        createSeedQualification(\n                \"QVS-2024-BSC-8891\",\n                \"Sarah Jenkins\",\n                \"STU-990142\",\n                \"Bachelor of Science in Software Engineering\",\n                \"DevOps & Cloud Computing\",\n                \"First Class Honours\",\n                LocalDate.of(2024, 7, 15),\n                inst1,\n                QualificationStatus.ACTIVE,\n                null\n        );\n\n        createSeedQualification(\n                \"QVS-2023-MSC-4412\",\n                \"David Miller\",\n                \"STU-881230\",\n                \"Master of Science in Cybersecurity\",\n                \"Information Security & Cryptography\",\n                \"Distinction\",\n                LocalDate.of(2023, 11, 20),\n                inst1,\n                QualificationStatus.ACTIVE,\n                null\n        );\n\n        createSeedQualification(\n                \"QVS-2022-DIP-1109\",\n                \"Marcus Vance\",\n                \"STU-772911\",\n                \"Diploma in Enterprise Systems Administration\",\n                \"Infrastructure Management\",\n                \"Upper Second Class\",\n                LocalDate.of(2022, 6, 30),\n                inst2,\n                QualificationStatus.REVOKED,\n                \"Issued in error - Academic misconduct disciplinary ruling\"\n        );\n    }\n\n    private void seedZimbabweStateUniversities() {\n        // =========================================================================\n        // 1. Zimbabwe Open University (ZOU)\n        // Specific requirement: IT degrees format ITM 190020, PGDE format EH250001 (first 2 digits = year)\n        // =========================================================================\n        Institution zou = seedInstitutionWithOfficer(\n                \"Zimbabwe Open University\",\n                \"ZOU-004\",\n                \"registry@zou.ac.zw\",\n                \"https://www.zou.ac.zw\",\n                \"officer_zou\",\n                \"ZOU Academic Registrar Officer\"\n        );\n\n        List<SeedRecord> zouRecords = List.of(\n                // IT Degrees: format ITM 190020 etc.\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2023-ITM-190020\", \"Itai Muringani\", \"ITM 190020\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Information Technology\", \"Network Administration & Cloud Systems\",\n                        \"First Class Honours\", LocalDate.of(2023, 11, 24), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2024-ITM-200021\", \"Rutendo Chitepo\", \"ITM 200021\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Network Computing\", \"Cybersecurity & Systems Infrastructure\",\n                        \"Upper Second Class (2.1)\", LocalDate.of(2024, 11, 22), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2025-ITM-210022\", \"Memory Mandaza\", \"ITM 210022\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Software Engineering\", \"Enterprise Application Development\",\n                        \"First Class Honours\", LocalDate.of(2025, 5, 18), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2026-ITM-220023\", \"Kuda Marange\", \"ITM 220023\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Multimedia Technology\", \"Digital Media & Interactive Web\",\n                        \"Upper Second Class (2.1)\", LocalDate.of(2026, 3, 10), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2023-ITM-190024\", \"Learnmore Zimunya\", \"ITM 190024\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Management Information Systems\", \"Enterprise Database Administration\",\n                        \"Lower Second Class (2.2)\", LocalDate.of(2023, 11, 24), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n\n                // PGDE Degrees: format EH250001 where the first 2 digits are the year\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2025-PGDE-EH250001\", \"Sekai Mataranyika\", \"EH250001\",\n                        \"Postgraduate Diploma in Education (Mathematics)\", \"Secondary Mathematics Pedagogy\",\n                        \"Distinction\", LocalDate.of(2025, 11, 28), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2024-PGDE-EH240002\", \"Tapiwa Rusike\", \"EH240002\",\n                        \"Postgraduate Diploma in Education (Science)\", \"Integrated Sciences Pedagogy\",\n                        \"Merit\", LocalDate.of(2024, 11, 22), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2023-PGDE-EH230003\", \"Grace Mukaro\", \"EH230003\",\n                        \"Postgraduate Diploma in Education (English Language)\", \"Applied Linguistics & Literature Pedagogy\",\n                        \"Distinction\", LocalDate.of(2023, 11, 24), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2022-PGDE-EH220004\", \"Admire Charamba\", \"EH220004\",\n                        \"Postgraduate Diploma in Education (Educational Leadership)\", \"School Administration & Supervision\",\n                        \"Merit\", LocalDate.of(2022, 11, 25), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"ZOU-2021-PGDE-EH210005\", \"Patience Mutungwazi\", \"EH210005\",\n                        \"Postgraduate Diploma in Education (ICT in Education)\", \"Instructional Media & E-Learning\",\n                        \"Pass\", LocalDate.of(2021, 11, 26), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null)\n        );\n        batchSaveQualifications(zou, zouRecords);\n\n        // =========================================================================\n        // 2. University of Zimbabwe (UZ)\n        // =========================================================================\n        Institution uz = seedInstitutionWithOfficer(\n                \"University of Zimbabwe\",\n                \"UZ-001\",\n                \"registrar@uz.ac.zw\",\n                \"https://www.uz.ac.zw\",\n                \"officer_uz\",\n                \"UZ Academic Registrar Officer\"\n        );\n\n        List<SeedRecord> uzRecords = List.of(\n                new SeedRecord(\"UZ-2024-BSC-3112\", \"Tendai Moyo\", \"R203112B\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Computer Science\", \"Artificial Intelligence & Distributed Systems\",\n                        \"First Class Honours\", LocalDate.of(2024, 7, 12), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"UZ-2023-BSC-2034\", \"Chipo Dube\", \"R192034A\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Science Honours in Civil Engineering\", \"Structural Engineering & Hydraulics\",\n                        \"Upper Second Class (2.1)\", LocalDate.of(2023, 7, 14), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE, null),\n                new SeedRecord(\"UZ-2024-MED-4512\", \"Farai Ncube\", \"R184512M\",\n                        \"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery (MBChB)\", \"General Medicine & Clinical Surgery\",\n                        \"Honours\", LocalDate.of(2024, 12, 5), QualificationStatus.ACTIVE